            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28903",
            "title": "Map alpha and colorspace attributes to web features",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-25T18:10:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-24T08:02:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "nt1m",
                "url": "https://github.com/nt1m"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome is updating the device memory limits, removing older limits and adding newer ones. It would be good to document what limits are supported.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Difficult to test all memory types without access to devices of all memory type but here's proof that the 8GB cap no longer applies:<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/539919768-6d815170-aa1d-4664-9889-02f54c6a5665.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..V1ZVgG-nX8Hxq9SMG2LWecuPxuoTfCRxOyn8OonBncI\"><img width=\"773\" height=\"252\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/539919768-6d815170-aa1d-4664-9889-02f54c6a5665.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..V1ZVgG-nX8Hxq9SMG2LWecuPxuoTfCRxOyn8OonBncI\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 252px;\"></a></p>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6330376953921536\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6330376953921536</a>.<br>\nAvailable in Chrome 146 onwards (will be in Chrome Canary after this weekend)</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">MDN PR: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3848775679\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42887\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42887/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42887\">mdn/content#42887</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28900",
            "title": "Update device memory limits",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-27T14:43:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-23T19:28:04.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "tunetheweb",
                "url": "https://github.com/tunetheweb"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">… value</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 144 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">maintain-framerate-and-resolution</code> value of the <a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/mst-content-hint/#dom-rtcdegradationpreference\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCDegradationPreference</code></a> dictionary, which is used in the options object of the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCRtpSender/setParameters\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCRtpSender.setParameters()</code></a> method, and available in the return value of the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCRtpSender/getParameters\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCRtpSender.getParameters()</code></a> method.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5156290162720768\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5156290162720768</a> for the release details.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a sub-data point to each method's data structure for this new value.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28898",
            "title": "Chrome 144 RTCDegradationPreference maintain-framerate-and-resolution…",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-24T16:01:10.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-23T18:13:41.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 144 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">ch-ua-high-entropy-values</code> <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Permissions-Policy\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy</code></a> directive. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6176703867781120\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6176703867781120</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for the feature itself, and a note to the <code class=\"notranslate\">NavigatorUAData.getHighEntropyValues()</code> data point to state that this feature can be controlled by the new policy.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28895",
            "title": "Chrome 144 supports ch-ua-high-entropy-values permissions policy",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-24T16:05:10.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-23T11:30:37.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        }
